Subject: [PATCH] libbpf: provide 128-bit aliases in the private Linux types header

The Linux 7.3 ARM64 UAPI uses __u128 from linux/types.h in asm/ptrace.h.
libbpf shadows linux/types.h with its private wrapper, which includes only
asm/types.h and therefore misses these aliases. Mirror the UAPI typedefs
when the compiler supports 128-bit integers, preserving 16-byte alignment.
This compatibility patch is selected only for SR1010 builds.

--- a/include/linux/types.h
+++ b/include/linux/types.h
@@ -11,6 +11,11 @@
 
 #include <asm/types.h>
 #include <asm/posix_types.h>
+
+#ifdef __SIZEOF_INT128__
+typedef __signed__ __int128 __s128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+typedef unsigned __int128 __u128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+#endif
 
 #define __bitwise__
 #define __bitwise __bitwise__
